%I A398346 #25 Oct 04 2026 20:45:00
%S A398346 15,18,45,225,675,1125,3375,5625,7875
%N A398346 Numbers with at least two digits, whose second and last digits are nonzero, that divide every number obtained by inserting any number of 0's between their first and second digits.
%C A398346 Finite and full. Proof: write k = a*10^m + t with leading digit a and tail t < 10^m. Inserting a further zero sends N to 10*N - 9*t, so k divides all insertions iff k | 9*t. Then 9*t = c*k with 1 <= c <= 8, so t*(9-c) = c*a*10^m. As 10 does not divide t, 9-c must absorb all of 2^m or all of 5^m, forcing m <= 3; checking these cases gives the nine terms.
%C A398346 15, 18, 45 are the elastic numbers without a zero digit (A285176), i.e., the base-10 seeds counted by A394974(10) = 3.
%D A398346 Daniel Griller, Elastic Numbers: 108 Puzzles for the Serious Problem Solver, Rational Falcon, 2017, ISBN 978-0-9957826-0-0.
%H A398346 Robert Bilinski, <a href="https://cms.math.ca/wp-content/uploads/crux-pdfs/CRUXv41n3.pdf">The Contest Corner: solution to problem CC111 (Problem A1 of the 2003 Mexican Mathematical Olympiad)</a>, Crux Mathematicorum 41(3) (2015), 97-98.
%F A398346 The terms are the numbers k = a*10^m + t (a = leading digit, t = tail) with 9*t = c*k for some 1 <= c <= 8.
%F A398346 For c = 1 one has k = (9/8)*a*10^m, which gives 45 = (9/8)*40, 225 = (9/8)*200, 675 = (9/8)*600, and 1125*d for d = 1, 3, 5, 7.
%F A398346 The remaining terms are 15 (c = 3) and 18 (c = 4).
%e A398346 675 is a term: 675 divides 6075 = 675*9, 60075 = 675*89, 600075 = 675*889, and so on.
%e A398346 1125 is a term: 1125 divides 10125 = 1125*9, 100125 = 1125*89, and so on.
%o A398346 (Python)
%o A398346 def ok(m, a, c):
%o A398346     num, den = c*a*10**m, 9-c
%o A398346     if num % den: return None
%o A398346     t = num // den
%o A398346     return a*10**m + t if 10**(m-1) <= t < 10**m and t % 10 else None
%o A398346 print(sorted({x for m in range(1, 10) for a in range(1, 10) for c in range(1, 9) if (x := ok(m, a, c))}))
%Y A398346 Cf. A285176, A394974.
%K A398346 nonn,base,fini,full,new
%O A398346 1,1
%A A398346 _Karan Sharma_, Sep 29 2026
